1
00:00:00,321 --> 00:00:01,910
Your plane takes off...

2
00:00:01,910 --> 00:00:02,670
and your ears

3
00:00:02,670 --> 00:00:03,372
go...

4
00:00:03,372 --> 00:00:04,160
POP!

5
00:00:04,337 --> 00:00:05,560
Relax.

6
00:00:05,560 --> 00:00:07,167
Your ear just burped.

7
00:00:07,210 --> 00:00:08,210
Behind your eardrum

8
00:00:08,210 --> 00:00:08,983
is a tiny

9
00:00:08,983 --> 00:00:10,133
pocket of air.

10
00:00:10,180 --> 00:00:11,230
As you climb,

11
00:00:11,230 --> 00:00:12,793
cabin pressure drops...

12
00:00:12,793 --> 00:00:13,523
so that air

13
00:00:13,523 --> 00:00:14,733
swells...

14
00:00:14,770 --> 00:00:15,898
until a tiny tube

15
00:00:15,898 --> 00:00:17,350
to the back of your nose

16
00:00:17,350 --> 00:00:19,200
burps the extra out.

17
00:00:19,236 --> 00:00:19,654
Landing

18
00:00:19,654 --> 00:00:20,667
is worse.

19
00:00:20,720 --> 00:00:21,517
Now the pocket

20
00:00:21,517 --> 00:00:22,375
shrinks...

21
00:00:22,375 --> 00:00:23,067
and the suction

22
00:00:23,067 --> 00:00:24,089
clamps that tube

23
00:00:24,089 --> 00:00:24,800
shut.

24
00:00:24,850 --> 00:00:25,934
So you swallow,

25
00:00:25,934 --> 00:00:26,933
or yawn...

26
00:00:26,990 --> 00:00:28,023
and a little muscle

27
00:00:28,023 --> 00:00:29,625
yanks it open.

28
00:00:29,670 --> 00:00:30,569
Babies can't do that

29
00:00:30,569 --> 00:00:31,720
on purpose.

30
00:00:31,720 --> 00:00:32,850
But crying...

31
00:00:32,850 --> 00:00:34,233
can open it too.

32
00:00:34,436 --> 00:00:35,956
So that screaming baby

33
00:00:35,956 --> 00:00:37,380
in row twelve?

34
00:00:37,380 --> 00:00:38,750
Technically...

35
00:00:38,750 --> 00:00:40,033
doing it right.

36
00:00:40,890 --> 00:00:41,820
Next up:

37
00:00:41,820 --> 00:00:42,644
why sunlight

38
00:00:42,644 --> 00:00:43,492
makes some of us

39
00:00:43,492 --> 00:00:44,180
sneeze.

40
00:00:44,490 --> 00:00:45,560
Subscribe...

41
00:00:45,560 --> 00:00:46,730
bless you.

